meta {
  name: Delete the abandoned asset
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/library/assets/{{abandonedAssetId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}

docs {
  Deleting an asset marks it deleted; the row stays. Content items point at
  assets, and a row that vanishes takes the meaning of those pointers with it:
  an item would still name an asset id that resolves to nothing, which reads as
  corruption rather than as a decision somebody made.

  What the tombstone is worth is visible in folder 11. A placement whose
  content item hangs off a deleted asset resolves to source_deleted, which is a
  different answer from "not indexed" and needs different handling.

  Deleting an already deleted asset is 204 as well. Delete is a statement about
  where things should end up, not about what state they were in.
}
